  "equipment_type": "Soft starter (motor control)",
  "applies_to": "ABB PSE18...PSE370 softstarters using the internal Modbus RTU interface (Modbus RTU adaptor on the front fieldbus connector), document 1SFC132367M0201 Rev B.",
  "summary": "ABB's compact PSE softstarters can be controlled over Modbus RTU through a small adaptor on their fieldbus port. Status comes as discrete inputs or one status word, measurements (currents, frequency, power factor, starts, run time) as 16-bit registers, and the motor is started and stopped through coils or a control word. Start/stop and protection settings are directly readable and writable as one register each. This map covers the full published register set.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 255,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "All addresses are printed as hex protocol addresses and go on the wire unchanged; the manual's example frames send 0000h (coils), 0100h, 0202h, 2000h and 3007h exactly as listed. So 0202h is requested as 514 decimal."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Softstarter type PSE - Fieldbus Communication, Internal Modbus RTU",
    "doc_number": "1SFC132367M0201 Rev B",
    "revision_date": "2019-12-18",
    "url": "https://www.precision-elec.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/11/PSE18-370-Fieldbus-Communication-Internal-Modbus-RTU-PSE.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "p. 3 (enable parameters), pp. 5-8 (coils, status and control word), p. 9 (analog inputs), pp. 9-11 (diagnostics), pp. 12-13 (parameters, baud register), pp. 15-20 (example frames)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "This copy is hosted by the US distributor Precision Electric; it is the unaltered ABB document (ABB footer, document ID 1SFC132367M0201 Rev B). ABB's online library did not return a copy for this document ID.",
    "All values are 16-bit. Read-only data blocks (status word, analog inputs, diagnostics, Modbus diagnostics) answer both function 03 and 04; they are listed as input registers here. The digital input telegram answers function 01 or 02 and is listed as discrete inputs; the output coils can be read back with 01/02.",
    "Scaling follows the manual's 'Value = 1 => ...' column: power factor 100 = 1, number of starts 1 = 100 starts, run time 1 = 10 h.",
    "Defaults: unit_id 255 is the parameter-list default of 3017h Fieldbus address (the manual's examples use 47); baud 19200 and 8E1 are the defaults of 301Dh/301Eh.",
    "Parameters 3016h-301Eh are read-only over Modbus; set them on the softstarter. 4064h lets the master change the baud rate.",
    "Left out: 2001h and 2002h (all bits reserved), the identification strings at 4000h-4017h (vendor, product code, revision, URL, product name; byte order of the text is not stated) and the reserved blocks. Function 43 (2Bh) Read Device Identification is also supported.",
    "Start/stop can come from coils 0101h/0102h (with auto mode on coil 0105h) or from bits 1/2 of the control word (with auto mode in bit 5). Setting auto mode in both places makes the device ignore start/stop."
  ],
